vendor/

Third-party source compiled into the benchmark. Currently: Lua.

The default build (make) compiles vendor/*.c into a static iblua.a and
links it, so the tool is self-contained and reproducible. This directory ships
empty -- populate it once:
    scripts/fetch-lua.sh            # latest pinned version (5.4.x)
    scripts/fetch-lua.sh 5.4.7      # a specific version


The Makefile excludes lua.c and luac.c from liblua.a (each defines its own
main() -- the standalone interpreter and the bytecode compiler).

Prefer not to vendor? Build against a system Lua instead:

make LUA_SYS=1                  # uses pkg-config for lua5.4 / lua

Vendored *.c / *.h / *.o and liblua.a are git-ignored (see .gitignore).
